          "notes": "Formatting-helper migration complete. 285 toFixed()/toLocaleString() call sites across 70 files identified (outside src/lib/format.js). All 70 files processed across 2 sessions (7 in the first partial commit 9ee399b7, 63 in this session via 3 parallel batch passes): money/percent/R display sites migrated to formatCurrency/formatPercent/formatR; non-financial sites (dates, ratios without a design-system convention, durations, counts, fractional shares, chart-data props, CSV exports per format.js's own documented exemption, FX rates, abbreviated axis/gauge/peak-value notation, operational/infra cost amounts) left out of scope or allow-listed with reasoning in docs/design/2026-09-28__release-v9.8/ST-01-formatting-migration-allowlist.md. Also fixed 19 total pre-existing zero-P&L/zero-delta neutral-tone colour violations (AC bullet 2) opportunistically across the touched files (6 in the first partial commit; 13 more in this session's batches, e.g. MonthlyHeatmap.js, PlanVsReality.js, PositionModal.js, RMultipleDistribution.js, CohortAnalysis.js, JournalView.js, PerformanceSummary.js, MarketComparison.js x1, ExitReasonTable.js x2, PaperAccountPanel.js, TradeReflection.js x2, TagPerformance.js x2, TradeReflectionModal.js, BestWorstTrades.js, TradeBreakdown.js). One out-of-scope finding (RecentTradesWidget.js icon-badge colour, not a toFixed call site) filed as BLG-FE-192 rather than fixed in-line. New Playwright coverage: tests/e2e/st01-v98-formatting-migration.spec.js (SC-ST01-01/02), passes locally (2/2); representative sample per CLAUDE.md §2, not exhaustive per-file coverage."
